From: Yuya Hamamachi <yuya.hamamachi.sx@renesas.com>
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] ipa: camera_sensor_helper: Add black level for imx477

The RPP-X1 BlackLevelCorrection algorithm requires the camera sensor
helper to provide the black level, and fails to initialize otherwise,
which makes the whole IPA initialization fail.

Set the imx477 black level to 4096 (16-bit scale), the value used by the
Raspberry Pi tuning files for the imx477.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
index 3e13a84..8f0cc8a 100644
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -702,6 +702,7 @@ public:
 	{
 		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 0, 1024, -1, 1024 };
 		exposureMargin_ = 22;
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
 	}
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx477", CameraSensorHelperImx477)
